WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:25.947
In 1886 Gustave Eiffel, a very famous French builder, was chosen to build a tower in Paris for the 1889 International Exposition.

2
00:00:25.948 --> 00:00:30.980
However, when people first saw his drawings, they were not pleased.

3
00:00:30.981 --> 00:00:36.572
In fact, many people truly hated the new tower.

4
00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:41.012
"What is this?" asked a famous artist.

5
00:00:41.013 --> 00:00:47.966
"It is a picture of the new tower they are building for the International Exposition," replied his friend.

6
00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:49.376
"Do you like it?"

7
00:00:49.377 --> 00:00:53.640
"No," declared the artist, "I hate it.

8
00:00:53.641 --> 00:00:57.799
It is the strangest-looking tower I have ever seen.

9
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:04.262
It has no beauty and it will ruin Paris."

10
00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:08.663
Around Paris, other people were saying the same thing.

11
00:01:08.664 --> 00:01:17.197
"The tower that Gustave Eiffel is building looks like a big streetlamp," wrote one newspaper reporter.

12
00:01:17.198 --> 00:01:22.509
"Eiffel is building a factory pipe," wrote another reporter.

13
00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:30.676
Many of the artists and other important people wrote letters demanding that the Eiffel Tower not be built.

14
00:01:30.677 --> 00:01:36.344
They believed that Paris was too great a city for such a horrible tower.

15
00:01:36.345 --> 00:01:43.940
But thankfully, the people in charge did not listen to these complaints.

16
00:01:43.941 --> 00:01:50.103
Gustave Eiffel was one of the first builders to use metal in his constructions.

17
00:01:50.104 --> 00:01:56.868
He was famous for building large and strong bridges and tall buildings made of metal.

18
00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:05.884
Before building the Eiffel Tower, he also designed and built the Statue of Liberty in New York City.

19
00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:12.868
On July 1, 1887 Eiffel and his company began working on the tower.

20
00:02:12.869 --> 00:02:21.142
It was a very unusual building project because they first made all the pieces of the tower in a factory.

21
00:02:21.143 --> 00:02:28.804
Then they brought the pieces to Paris and put them together like a puzzle.

22
00:02:28.805 --> 00:02:34.202
Each piece of the puzzle was put together with special nails called rivets.

23
00:02:34.203 --> 00:02:39.493
The rivets were so large that it took four men to put one in.

24
00:02:39.494 --> 00:02:44.993
Since there were over two million rivets, this was a very big job.

25
00:02:44.994 --> 00:02:54.078
But slowly the pieces were put together, and the tower went up and up and up.

26
00:02:54.079 --> 00:02:59.872
By March 15, 1888, the workmen completed the first level.

27
00:02:59.873 --> 00:03:05.051
Then six months later, they had put the second level together.

28
00:03:05.052 --> 00:03:11.807
By March of 1889, the tower was completed and ready for the exposition.

29
00:03:11.808 --> 00:03:20.208
When it was finished, it was 324 meters tall and weighed more than 10,000 tons.

30
00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:25.950
When the Eiffel Tower was finished, the people of Paris were very pleased with it.

31
00:03:25.951 --> 00:03:34.735
Those who thought that the tower would look ugly, now thought it was one of the most wonderful structures ever made.

32
00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:45.932
Because the tower was made for visitors to the exposition, it needed to have elevators that could bring people up to the first, second, and top floors.

33
00:03:45.933 --> 00:03:52.727
Today that might seem easy, but in 1889 that was a very difficult job.

34
00:03:52.728 --> 00:03:57.170
No one had ever built elevators so high before.

35
00:03:57.171 --> 00:04:04.406
In most buildings, the elevators go straight up and straight down, but not in the Eiffel Tower.

36
00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:10.572
Because of the shape of the tower, the elevators had to travel along a curve.

37
00:04:10.573 --> 00:04:19.338
When people first saw these unusual elevators, they were amazed and excited.

38
00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:29.356
Because it was specifically built for the exposition, the Eiffel Tower was going to stay up for only a few years at first.

39
00:04:29.357 --> 00:04:35.796
But soon it became very popular and visitors from around the world came to see it.

40
00:04:35.797 --> 00:04:43.371
These days, over six million people visit the tower each year.

41
00:04:43.372 --> 00:04:50.036
So instead of taking the tower down, Gustave Eiffel found other good uses for the tower.

42
00:04:50.037 --> 00:04:55.225
In the early 1900s, there was a new invention called the radio.

43
00:04:55.226 --> 00:05:02.801
In order to travel far distances, radio signals must come from radio towers that are very tall.

44
00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:11.877
So Gustave had the great idea of using the Eiffel Tower as a radio tower.

45
00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:19.566
The Eiffel Tower is beautiful in the daytime because you can see the wonderful metal structure that Gustave built.

46
00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:29.151
However, it is also wondrous at night because there are more than 350 beautiful lights that cover it from head to toe.

47
00:05:29.152 --> 00:05:37.507
On top are two light beams that can be seen from over eighty kilometers away.
